    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d900">

                <pb facs="0737" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/7227</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr. Arredondo, representing
                        American interests</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 20, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reported <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Government is about to order
                    several thousand Mexican soldiers from Sonora to Chihuahua. Yaqui Valley
                    settlers fear campaign against Indians may be materially affected by such
                    action.</p>
                <pb facs="0738" n="662" xml:id="pg662"/>
                <p>Bring to attention appropriate authorities and express the hope of this
                    Government that campaign against Yaqui Indians be vigorously prosecuted and that
                    troops be not removed from Yaqui Valley.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
